    "description": "Typewriter Picatinny AFG: Laffs Dynamics\n\nPicatinny variant of the original Laffs Dynamics M-Lok Typewriter Foregrip. \n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 218C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16mm\nWall Thickness: .40mm\nWall Perimeters: 6+\nInfill: 32%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 18%\n\nPrint the AFG upside down.\n\nUse support blockers; as the inside of the foregrip is semi-hollow. \n\n\n\nHardware Needed: \n\n2x M4x30mm Bolt (Can be ground down to 28mm, so it doesn't stick out the side)\n\n2x M4 Hex Nut\n\n\n\nNotes:\n\n1) This has been designed as an AFG, intended to be used on smaller weapons such as PDWs and pistols to aid in safely \ncontrolling the weapon during firing. As of 2023; AFGs (Angled Foregrips) are still legal to use on handguns. \n\n\n\nAccreditations:\n\nSheridan: Requested a similar design to be made; which inspired this design's creation. Provided a base model to work from, \naiding in creating this design's overall dimensions to be similar to the Model 1928's foregrip. \n\nSelmon: Requested the picatinny variant of the original M-Lok Typewriter Foregrip. Offered payment; denied due to being a request and \nnot a formal contract. ",
